# G16 — the taper dichotomy becomes a theorem: no compactly supported taper can pass the gate

**The Riemann Hypothesis is not proved.**  Nothing was weakened and nothing was
assumed: `RiemannHypothesisFor`, `RiemannHypothesis`, `CompletedRiemannHypothesis`
and every earlier statement are untouched; there is no `sorry`/`admit`, no
`axiom`, no postulate, no Boolean receipt, no numerical evidence and no
`@[implemented_by]` in any Lean source.  `lake build RiemannAnalytic` succeeds
(8102 jobs, no warnings from project sources) and `#print axioms` on every new
theorem returns only `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.

G15 closed with one explicitly named open question.  Its §2 had proved the
source-normalization gate **red** for every taper whose transform decays only
polynomially along the prime frequencies `u = log n`, and observed that the sole
remaining possibility for a green gate was a taper transform decaying
*exponentially* at rate `> 1/2 + 2|α|` — i.e. a taper analytic in a horizontal
strip — which "appears incompatible with the compact support and plateau
hypotheses under which `finiteGridGramDefect_source_floor` proves the `L⁶`
floor".  That was recorded as an assessment, not a theorem.

**G16 turns it into a theorem, and closes the intermediate regime the G15
argument left uncovered.**

